cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "aggeodata: multi-source climate and soil data ingestion and datacube builder for agricultural research"
version: 0.2.7
date-released: 2026-11-20
abstract: >-
  aggeodata is a Python package that downloads daily climate and soil data
  (CHIRPS, CHIRTS, AgERA5, NASA POWER, SoilGrids) and builds analysis-ready
  NetCDF or Zarr datacubes aligned to a common grid and CRS. It can read
  cloud-optimized Zarr v3 mirrors on Hugging Face and the ECMWF ARCO store,
  and includes an MCP server for AI agents. It supports the CGIAR Climate
  Data Hub AI agent skills.
